(98, 'Nina Boldt, known mononymously and professionally as NINA (born 29 September 1983) is a German singer-songwriter based in London and Berlin. Her music is a fusion of pop, new wave, and electronic music. She released her debut album Sleepwalking in 2018 and her follow-up album Synthian in 2020. Her third major release Control (feat. Laura Fares) was released as an EP via Lakeshore Records and features samples from Cliff Martinez''s film score for Drive, which began a mainstream modern revival of the cliche 1980s music, art, and graphics scene.', '1983-09-29', 0),
