(1749, 'Raakhee Gulzar (née Majumdar) (Bengali pronunciation: [rakʰi], born 15 August 1940), professionally known as Raakhee, is an Indian actress who primarily works in Hindi and Bengali films. One of the leading and most popular actresses of the 1970s and early 1980s, Raakhee is a recipient of several awards including two National Film Awards and three Filmfare Awards. In 2003, she received Padma Shri, India''s fourth-highest civilian award.
