(2303, 'Daisy is a feminine given name. The flower name comes from the Old English word dægeseage, meaning "day''s eye". The name Daisy is therefore ultimately derived from this source. Daisy is also a nickname for Margaret because Marguerite, the French version of the latter name, is also a French name for the oxeye daisy.

', NULL, 0),
