(4179, 'Shreya Ghoshal (Bengali pronunciation: [ʃreja ɡʱoʃal], born 12 March 1984) is an Indian singer. Noted for her wide vocal range and versatility, she is one of the most prolific and influential  singers of India. Often referred to as the "Queen of Dynamics'''' for her remarkable vocal expressions, Ghoshal is widely regarded as one of the greatest vocalists of the Indian subcontinent. She has recorded songs for films and albums in various Indian and foreign languages and received numerous accolades, including five National Film Awards, four Kerala State Film Awards, two Tamil Nadu State Film Awards, one Maharashtra State Film Award, one Telangana Gaddar Film Award, two BFJA Awards, seven Filmfare Awards and ten Filmfare Awards South.
