(5231, 'Acharya Chinmoy Lahiri (Bengali: আচার্য চিন্ময় লাহিড়ী, 20 March 1920 – 17 August 1984) was an Indian vocalist from Bengal in the Hindustani classical tradition. He is known for the Khayal form of singing, as well as for his popular renditions of Dhrupad, Thumri and Tappa, along with Bengali Raga-pradhan songs.', NULL, 0),
