(11952, 'Lady Kash, born Kalaivani Nagaraj in 1990, is a Singaporean-Tamil rapper and songwriter.
Kash''s founded AKASHIK, her independent record label, in 2013. In 2018, she collaborated with Poongani Amma to release the bilingual hip-hop song "Villupaattu", which featured Villu Paatu (a type of storytelling through music).
In 2023, her hip-hop single, "Two Cents," was used in the Netflix comedy-drama series, Never Have I Ever.
Over the years, Kash has collaborated with composers such as A. R. Rahman, Yuvan Shankar Raja, Anirudh Ravichander, Santhosh Narayanan, Harris Jayaraj, and Thaman S.', NULL, 0),
(11953, 'Adele Laurie Blue Adkins (, born 5 May 1988) is an English singer-songwriter. Regarded as a British icon, she is known for her mezzo-soprano vocals and sentimental songwriting. Her accolades include 16 Grammy Awards, 12 Brit Awards (including three for British Album of the Year), an Academy Award, a Primetime Emmy Award, and a Golden Globe Award.
After graduating from the BRIT School in 2006, Adele signed a record deal with XL Recordings. Her debut album, 19 (2008), included the UK top-five singles "Chasing Pavements" and "Make You Feel My Love", becoming one of best-selling debut albums ever in the UK. She received the Grammy Award for Best New Artist. Adele''s second studio album, 21 (2011), became the best-selling album of the 21st century. 21 holds the record for the top-performing album in US chart history, topping the Billboard 200 for 24 weeks, with the singles "Rolling in the Deep", "Someone like You", and "Set Fire to the Rain" heading charts worldwide, becoming her signature s', '1988-05-05', 0),
(11954, NULL, NULL, 0),
